  "title": "Bridge2AI Releases Flagship AI-Ready Type 2 Diabetes Dataset",
  "bodyHtml": "<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">The Bridge2AI Artificial Intelligence Ready and Equitable Atlas for Diabetes Insights (</span><a style=\"text-decoration:none;\" href=\"https://aireadi.org/\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(17, 85, 204);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><u>AI-READI</u></span></a><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">) project, which aims to understand the development and reversal of type 2 diabetes, released a publicly available flagship type 2 diabetes dataset optimized for artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) applications. The dataset includes fourteen domains of data collected from 1,067 diverse human participants, who are a subset of the projected 4,000-participant total cohort. The cohort is designed to maximize diversity and minimize biases in order to promote ethical AI/ML modeling. The dataset is available&nbsp;</span><a style=\"text-decoration:none;\" href=\"https://fairhub.io/datasets/2\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(17, 85, 204);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><u>here</u></span></a><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">.</span></p>",
  "summary": "The Bridge2AI Artificial Intelligence Ready and Equitable Atlas for Diabetes Insights (AI-READI) project released a publicly available flagship type 2 diabetes dataset optimized for artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) applications.",
